{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>They fled at their voice.</b> It should have said 'מִקּוֹלָם' ('from their voice'), and furthermore — to where did they flee, and whither would they flee from before Him, blessed be He? Now, our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Tanchuma, Korach 11) that Korah and his assembly would constantly say: Moses is truth and his Torah is truth, and we are fabricators. And that voice began to echo forth immediately after the swallowing. And to that voice emerging from the place of swallowing, all Israel fled — to hear what they would say, for they assumed surely they were confessing their sin, and they wanted to know what was the essence of their sin, so that they would know to guard themselves from it, lest this cup pass over them too. And this is what it says: 'כִּי אָמְרוּ פֶּן תִּבְלָעֵנוּ הָאָרֶץ' ('for they said, lest the earth swallow us'). And from the fact that they said 'Moses is truth and his Torah is truth,' infer from this that they had also denied his Torah. And perhaps they predicated this on what they heard — 'אָנֹכִי' and 'לֹא יִהְיֶה לְךָ' — from the mouth of the Gevurah; if so, HaShem wants all Israel to hear everything from the mouth of the Gevurah, and whatever Moses further declares to them is nothing at all — to give room for his words which they too did not hear. And in my opinion, this is the intent of Rashi, who explained 'כִּי כָל הָעֵדָה כֻּלָּם קְדוֹשִׁים' — 'not you alone heard אָנֹכִי and לֹא יִהְיֶה לְךָ.' They meant by this: since the entire assembly also heard these two commandments, if HaShem desired commandments beyond these at present, why did He not make us hear such? Rather, surely from your own hearts you fabricate everything. And because they disputed the Torah, they said in their confession: Moses is truth and his Torah is truth."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:41:45.975421029Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}